<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · deity</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nandi (Hinduism)</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nandi is the sacred bull who serves as the mount and gatekeeper of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hindu</a> god <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shiva">Shiva</a>. Statues of a seated Nandi face the sanctum in most Shiva temples, and the bull appears on the coins of many dynasties devoted to Shiva, from the Kushans and Kushano-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sasanian-empire">Sasanians</a> to the Hindu Shahis, whose bull-and-horseman type was widely copied. Some traditions also treat Nandi as a sage and teacher.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nandi-hinduism.jpg" alt="Nandi (Hinduism)" width="320" height="374" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nandieshvara.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Shaka ruled harshly, and the massacres that followed the death of his mother <b>Nandi</b> in 1827 alienated many followers.</blockquote><a href="/empire/zulu-kingdom">Zulu Kingdom · Governance &amp; Law</a></li><li><blockquote>Shashanka was a Shaiva, and his gold coins show Shiva with his bull <b>Nandi</b>.</blockquote><a href="/state/gauda-kingdom">Gauda Kingdom</a></li><li><blockquote>Their silver 'bull and horseman' coins, showing Shiva's bull <b>Nandi</b> and a mounted warrior, were imitated widely across northern India and Central Asia.</blockquote><a href="/state/hindu-shahis">Hindu Shahis</a></li><li><blockquote>The Kushanshahs issued gold and copper coins in the Kushan style, often showing the god Oesho (Shiva) with the bull <b>Nandi</b>, alongside Sasanian crowns and Middle Persian or Bactrian legends.</blockquote><a href="/state/kushano-sasanian-kingdom">Kushano-Sasanian Kingdom</a></li></ul></section>
